---
import Image from "astro/components/Image.astro";
import Content from "../Content.astro";
import SectionHead from "../SectionHead.astro";
import cntl from "cntl";
import ProjectPubs from "../../layouts/ProjectPubs.astro";
import PubButton from "../buttons/PubButton.astro";
import herbarium from "../../assets/img/herbarium.jpg";
import outreach from "../../assets/img/hh-lsu_outreach.webp";
import patah from "../../assets/img/mt-patah.webp";

const spaceClasses = cntl`
  mr-1
`;

const pillars = [
  {
    title: "Specimen acquisition",
    text: "Targeted fieldwork in under-sampled biodiversity hotspots of the Indo-Australian Archipelago, with best-practice specimen and tissue preservation and photographs and recordings linked to each voucher in the field.",
  },
  {
    title: "Stewardship & data",
    text: "FAIR, Darwin Core–ready data from the field onward. NAHPU, our cross-platform digital field catalog, supports QR/barcode scanning and is adding automatic validation to streamline the path from field to collection database.",
  },
  {
    title: "Training & outreach",
    text: "Collecting while training local students closest to the field sites, and explicitly crediting the communities, guides, and porters who make remote expeditions possible.",
  },
];
---

<div>
  <SectionHead text="Natural history collections" />
  <Content>
    <p>
      Continuously growing collections keep natural history museums relevant:
      newly acquired specimens are the best material for genomic, microbiome,
      and phenomic studies, and many regions remain poorly documented. Over 13
      years, my work has both drawn on existing museum collections and built
      new ones, expanding sampling to under-surveyed islands and mountains.
    </p>
  </Content>

  <div class="mt-6 grid gap-4 md:grid-cols-3">
    {
      pillars.map((p) => (
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-moss-900/15 bg-white p-4 dark:border-moss-100/15 dark:bg-forest-950">
          <h3 class="font-serif text-lg text-forest-900 dark:text-forest-100">{p.title}</h3>
          <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-forest-800 dark:text-forest-200">{p.text}</p>
        </div>
      ))
    }
  </div>

  <SectionHead text="Local communities in the field" />
  <Content>
    <Image
      src={patah}
      alt="Field camp in mossy montane forest on Mt. Patah, Sumatra"
      width={340}
      class="float-right mb-2 ml-4 mt-2 rounded-xl"
    />
    <p>
      Exploration narratives too often center on the researchers. In 2023, I
      led a four-month expedition to three mountains on Sumatra that involved
      more than 40 local residents at each site. Without them, we could never
      have carried roughly 800 kilograms of field supplies and food up each
      mountain, and some of them collected specimens alongside us. Biodiversity
      research is a collaborative, global effort, and local communities are
      rightful stakeholders in discovery.
    </p>
  </Content>

  <SectionHead text="Public engagement" />
  <Content>
    <Image
      src={outreach}
      alt="Showing collection specimens and field tools at an LSU Museum of Natural Science outreach event"
      width={300}
      class="float-left mb-2 mr-4 mt-2 rounded-xl"
    />
    <p>
      Museums are critical interfaces between scientific discovery and public
      literacy. At outreach events, such as those at the LSU Museum of Natural
      Science, I share representative specimens from our collections and the
      tools we use in the field.
    </p>
  </Content>
  <div class="clear-both"></div>

<Image
src={herbarium}
alt="Herbarium Universitas Andalas"
width={220}
class="rounded-xl float-right ml-4 mt-8"
/>
<SectionHead text="Herbarium digitization and data mobilization" />
<Content>
<p>
  This project is led by Dr. Nurainas at the Herbarium Universitas Andalas
  (ANDA) funded through the collection and data mobilization grant provided by
  the Global Biodiversity Information Facility (GBIF). We digitized >65,000
  sheets of the herbarium specimens at ANDA and make the data accessible
  through the GBIF portal.
</p>
<div class="mt-4 mb-2 text-semibold">Published datasets:</div>
<ProjectPubs author="Nurainas et. al.">
  <PubButton
    author="Nurainas N, Amolia R R, Taufiq A, Handika H, Syamsuardi S"
    year="2024a"
    title="Flora of Sumatra : Vascular plant collection from Batang Toru Forest deposited in ANDA Herbarium"
    doi="https://doi.org/10.15468/ue7xyn"
  />
  <span class={spaceClasses}>,</span>
  <PubButton
    author="Nurainas N, Taufiq A, Handika H, Syamsuardi S"
    year="2024b"
    title="Flora of Sumatra: Vascular plant collection of selected families deposited at Herbarium of Andalas University (ANDA)"
    doi="https://doi.org/10.15468/sncpxn"
  />
  <span class={spaceClasses}>,</span>
  <PubButton
    author="Nurainas N, Taufiq A, Handika H, Harapan T S, Syamsuardi S"
    year="2024c"
    title="Flora Sumatra: Digitizing and data basing specimens of the Sumatran Flora deposited at Herbarium Universitas Andalas (ANDA)-Part 2"
    doi="https://doi.org/10.15468/55evew "
  />
</ProjectPubs>
</Content>
</div>
